,151644,872,198,50,3948,279,3491,3019,553,3019,13,20678,697,1590,4226,304,1124,79075,90,1112,92,382,9885,678,6351,5109,400,89,3,1741,429,198,59,7265,90,6612,9,532,59,2359,91,1124,37018,90,89,481,220,19,15170,89,481,220,23,92,1124,1291,91,14581,220,16,11,90155,59,2359,91,1124,37018,90,89,481,220,16,17,15170,89,481,220,23,72,92,1124,1291,91,14581,1124,37018,90,20,15170,18,27275,59,408,90,6612,9,92,6269,678,279,9904,11,18663,553,76602,13,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nFind all complex numbers $z$ such that\n\\begin{align*}\n\\left| \\frac{z - 4}{z - 8} \\right| &= 1, \\\\\n\\left| \\frac{z - 12}{z - 8i} \\right| &= \\frac{5}{3}.\n\\end{align*}Enter all the solutions, separated by commas.","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"5618e45fbb00d0bfe32a1ab22abc3548de9cb2e55a52ab701bfcaafcf1d1ea4c"},"seconds":59.820942878723145,"seed":708186046405636734,"stop":"eos","text":"To solve for all complex numbers $z$ that satisfy the given equations, we can approach the problem step by step.\n\nFirst, the given equations are:\n\\[\n\\left| \\frac{z - 4}{z - 8} \\right| = 1\n\\]\nand\n\\[\n\\left| \\frac{z - 12}{z - 8i} \\right| = \\frac{5}{3}.\n\\]\n\n### Step 1: Interpret the first equation\nThe equation \\(\\left| \\frac{z - 4}{z - 8} \\right| = 1\\) implies that the distance from \\(z\\) to \\(4\\) is equal to the distance from \\(z\\) to \\(8\\). This means \\(z\\) lies on the perpendicular bisector of the line segment joining \\(4\\) and \\(8\\).\n\nThe midpoint of the segment from \\(4\\) to \\(8\\) is:\n\\[\n\\frac{4 + 8}{2} = 6.\n\\]\n\nThe perpendicular bisector is the vertical line \\(x = 6\\). So, \\(z\\) can be written as \\(z = 6 + bi\\) where \\(b\\) is a real number.\n\n### Step 2: Substitute \\(z = 6 + bi\\) into the second equation\nNow we substitute \\(z = 6 + bi\\) into the second equation:\n\\[\n\\left| \\frac{(6 + bi) - 12}{(6 + bi) - 8i} \\right| = \\frac{5}{3}.\n\\]\nThis simplifies to:\n\\[\n\\left| \\frac{-6 + bi}{6 + (b-8)i} \\right| = \\frac{5}{3}.\n\\]\nThe magnitudes of the numerator and the denominator are:\n\\[\n\\left| -6 + bi \\right| = \\sqrt{36 + b^2}\n\\]\nand\n\\[\n\\left| 6 + (b-8)i \\right| = \\sqrt{36 + (b-8)^2}.\n\\]\nThus, the equation becomes:\n\\[\n\\frac{\\sqrt{36 + b^2}}{\\sqrt{36 + (b-8)^2}} = \\frac{5}{3}.\n\\]\nSquaring both sides, we get:\n\\[\n\\frac{36 + b^2}{36 + (b-8)^2} = \\frac{25}{9}.\n\\]\nCross-multiplying gives:\n\\[\n9(36 + b^2) = 25(36 + (b-8)^2).\n\\]\nExpanding both sides, we get:\n\\[\n324 + 9b^2 = 900 + 25(b^2 - 16b + 64).\n\\]\nSimplifying further:\n\\[\n324 + 9b^2 = 900 + 25b^2 - 400b + 1600.\n\\]\nCombining like terms:\n\\[\n324 + 9b^2 = 2500 + 25b^2 - 400b.\n\\]\nRearranging all terms to one side:\n\\[\n0 = 16b^2 - 400b + 2176.\n\\]\nSimplifying by dividing by 16:\n\\[\nb^2 - 25b + 136 = 0.\n\\]\nWe solve this quadratic equation using the quadratic formula \\(b = \\frac{-B \\pm \\sqrt{B^2 - 4AC}}{2A}\\):\n\\[\nb = \\frac{25 \\pm \\sqrt{625 - 544}}{2} = \\frac{25 \\pm \\sqrt{81}}{2} = \\frac{25 \\pm 9}{2}.\n\\]\nThis gives us two solutions:\n\\[\nb = \\frac{34}{2} = 17 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad b = \\frac{16}{2} = 8.\n\\]\nThus, the solutions for \\(z\\) are:\n\\[\nz = 6 + 17i \\quad \\text{and} \\quad z = 6 + 8i.\n\\]\n\nThe final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{6 + 17i, 6 + 8i}.\n\\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{6 + 17i, 6 + 8i}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
